olutely  going to get out there's no way that it  won't be spoiled and i'm shocked that it  didn't and i'm so happy because the fans  went  crazy also in the season 17 premiere joe  and jackson have a hilarious hilarious  sexy kiss people is a sexy kiss  where joe ends up crying what was it  like filming that scene with jesse  williams  so jesse and i have wanted to work  together for a really long time and so  we've been begging for scenes together  this is what we end up getting  we read it together at the table read  and we could not stop laughing it was  really funny and then when we actually  filmed the scene we also couldn't stop  laughing because  we improvised a little bit and it's just  really funny the writing was really  funny there was a moment where  like little things happened that made us  laugh like he hands me back the vodka  bottle that she had and it kind of hit  my hand away and it went all over my  face and then the yellow cat  were like no keep it in it's already so  awkward just keep it in  so we had a lot of fun filming that  scene joe arrived on grace during season  nine  is that any character that you wish joe  could have met from the earlier seasons  okay my husband knows this so it's okay  for me to say this but i have a huge  crush on kyle chandler i know he was  pink mist in the bomb episode so it  ended badly for him but i wish i'd had  one scene  just one scene with him one of the best  grey's anatomy episodes is silent all  these years  when joe helps a sexual assault survivor  what was it like filming that scene in  the hallway with all the women of gray  sloane  that episode was incredibly intense that  scene in particular was really emotional  and what i love about the scene that  some people know  not everybody knows is that the women  lining our hallway were not just  background doctors or  actors you know any actors that we had  on the show um we had a lot of people  in all different kind of departments on  the show a lot of women that wanted to  be part of the whole way of women so  there's people that were in editing or  some of our producers it was an  incredible scene it was very emotional  for everybody that day  so it turned out to be a fantastic very  powerful scene i think spoke to a lot of  people  joe's backstory has slowly been revealed  to us  over the years how much of it did you  know going in nothing  is the answer i did not know anything  when did you find out joe's real name  i didn't know anything the episode where  i  was helping a homeless man that's when i  was told that she had been homeless they  were like oh by the way you were  homeless and i was like oh good to know  crazy thing about being on grey's  anatomy is that you find out as the show  goes on so i didn't know that i've been  married before i didn't know  the abuse of relationship there was so  much that got revealed over the seasons  so i did not know anything going into it  really and i found out joe's name  when i read the script do you have a  favorite joe and alex moment on grey's  anatomy  it's way back in season nine but the the  time that they got drunk together at the  bar  was so funny in the hotel and then  stealing over and  key that is still one of my favorite  scenes with joe and alex all the way  back in the day what's your role people  would be surprised to find out you  auditioned for so many roles would i  audition for  i think i did i think i did tweet this  but i auditioned  for belle in once upon a time and i  really wanted it because who didn't want  to be a disney princess and i did i was  so sad when i got it and then i got  grazed very soon after so  it was meant to be season 17 has been  tackling the coronavirus pandemic what  has it been like bringing this important  storyline to life it's very strange  because usually there's a separation  between our real lives and then  obviously going  and shooting the show and what's really  bizarre about filming the pandemic is  that we're still in  it so we're wearing the mask to work  we're washing our hands we're doing all  the things we're supposed to be doing  and you know obviously it's very scary  and then we get to work and we're  playing it out as  front line workers so it's a very  intense season  and you know it's it looks very  different on set we all have to stay six  feet apart  and you know abc and disney are taking  all the precautions necessary to keep us  all safe  but i think it's really important and i  i can tell from the fan reaction that  people are really  happy actually that we're that we're  giving this storyline this season  is there a grey's enemy cast group chat  or who do you talk to the most when  you're not  on set jessie captures one of my best  friends who plays arizona and she'll  always be part of gray so that will be  my answer  i text jake all the time and there's  no cast group chat there should be but i  think that we're all on individual chats  with each other  who is your dream gray's anatomy guesta  taylor swift i know she loves the show i  feel like she should just do  one episode i don't i don't know how it  would happen as a patient or she's a  doctor  but i think that she deserves to come on  and finally what tv show are you  currently obsessed with  okay guys i have just started i know i'm  late but the boys i don't know if you  guys are watching it it is  so good i want to be a member of the  seven  so bad whether i'm good or evil it's  amazing  i've binged it i actually have just one  episode to go which is the finale of  season two but it's incredible  i need to be part of that fandom too  thank you buzzfeed so much for having me  it was a pleasure answering all of your  fan questions do not forget to watch  grey's anatomy on abc  9 pm thursday nights  you
 

